WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You have a set.

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you get
to design a set.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
What did you want to represent
in the set

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're sitting down
and just think about visuall

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.073 size:84% position:42% line:92%
want you wanted to see?

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, man, I had no idea.
To be honest, I feel like --

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:09.743 line:92%
-I totally didn't either.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:12.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm pretty good at
visualizing what a script

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
is gonna turn into.
-Yes.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:14.948 line:92%
-What lyrics will turn into.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
The set was so out
of my comfort zone.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have no visual style.
-Oh, 100%.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-My set designer was like,

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
"And then this contraption
will open."

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.790
I'm like, "I have no clue what
you're saying to me right now.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm really happy with
how it turned out.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.761 size:88% position:44%
I think it's super cool.
It's modern. It's funky.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a little sneak peek
at the set.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.199
And then that --
Tell us a little bit about that.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.302
-So, on my desk I have
the two loves of my life.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.871 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So my dog, Scarborough.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.438 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And French fries.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, French fries
and Scarborough.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, correct.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.643
-I think a lot of people lov
French fries and their dog

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.245 line:92%
But they rarely have the photo

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.112 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Really? That's weird.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they never
have the frame.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.283
-And this is based on a true
story because for about a year

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.118 line:92%
I did have a framed picture of

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.387 size:78% position:39%
like, a Big Mac combo
on my night table.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:54.788 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.189 size:88% position:44%
-I thought it was, like,
aesthetically pleasing.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.123 line:92%
-Sure, they put a lot of wor

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.425
into making those Big Mac combos
look it.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're supposed to frame
pictures of things you love.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:01.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And so there you go.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-Yes.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.931 size:78% position:39%
-Scarborough is named
after your hometown?

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.635
-Yes. Scarborough is named after
my home town in Toronto.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.471 line:92%
I mean, can we take a moment

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:14.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only reason
I want to be successful

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.375 line:92%
is to give my dog a better life.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I swear, I'm obsessed.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you feel as though
at this point

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
he doesn't have
a good enough life?

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has he complained at all?
Has he --

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, he could have
more costumes.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.552
He could have a bigger yard.
He could have -- I just --

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think many -- I think
this is a photo of a dog,

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he hears you want to ge
him more costumes.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that is what they do
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:33.927 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I mean, he's so sweet.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He is very sweet.
-He's so, so sweet.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who are your guests
this first week?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.935
-So, this first week, our firs
show tonight, is Mindy Kaling.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Rainn Wilson.
-Excellent.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:47.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep. And then we've got
Kenan Thompson.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:47.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great.
-Yep.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the all-time greats.
-Yep.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
Got Chelsea Handler.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we got Tracee Ellis Ross,
so it's a stacked week.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.014 line:92%
-That's a very good first week

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.385
-You know, looking back,
one of my favorite things

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.355 size:84% position:42%
about that beginning
when you have a show --

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you've known --
So what have you known?

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.659
About six months that you've had
this coming, seven months?

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.427 line:92%
-Probably a little longer.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. So it's like
putting together a staff.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's one of
the most exciting things.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:11.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have all these slots
to fill.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it fun putting togethe
a writing staff?

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a double-edged sword
I mean, it's super cool

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:20.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I have more than
five people working on stuff

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:20.640 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.510
-But it's also --
I have no idea what anyone does.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:23.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yes.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:24.777 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You mean on your crew.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, 100%.
-Yeah.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Every day someone comes up to
me and says, "Hi, I'm Chad

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do something
with the script."

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "What do you do?
I have no idea."

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.085 line:92%
And I want to know so badl

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.953 size:81% position:41%
because I know they're
all working so hard.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.956
Another thing is because
I did everything by myself

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
for so long,
I have major trust issues.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, interesting.
-Like, 100%.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:41.628 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-That's what they say.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
People who start on YouTube,
they don't trust anyone.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.365 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.501
-When the prop department tell
me they're gonna make a prop

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.336 line:92%
I'm like, "But are you sure?

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.204 line:92%
Like, "Are you gonna do that?"

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a hard time believing
I don't have to do this.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:56.910
So I'm a little bit -- a littl
annoying to my staff, probably

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:57.577 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And what about writers?

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what were you lookin
for in writers?

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-'Cause that's another thing

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
You sort of wrote by yoursel
for all these years.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, for eight years
I was writing my own stuff

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now I have a writers' room
which is fantastic.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just need to humble-brag
for a second

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I think
it's very important.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.026
I was very adamant on having
an inclusive writers' room

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is very important to me
so it has over 50% women.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.631
-Congratulations. That's great
-And over 50% people of color.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.900
-That's awesome.
-And I was very adamant of that.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, I mean,
obviously when I go out there,

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
you'll get my point of view.
-Sure.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.005 line:92%
-You know, a woman of color.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.040 line:92%
But I think it's so importan

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get the point of view
of my writers

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:29.742 line:92%
because they're also so diverse.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.111
I mean, that's what storytelling
and TV should be about.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
It should be representativ
of the real world.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.415 line:92%
And I think that's so important.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I wanted
an inclusive writers' room

